{"content_hash": "8725d71f94945e97", "version_id": 894, "article_id": 90, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "John Lewis unveils 2026 Christmas ad, urging shoppers not to give up on gifting", "title_zh": "John Lewis发布2026圣诞广告，劝大家别放弃用心送礼", "has_translation": true, "topic": "lifestyle", "source": "toodaylab", "source_url": "https://www.toodaylab.com/84280", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784210156339-43fceaca3548?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8am9obiUyMGxld2lzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTQwMTMzNjd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Catarina Duarte on Unsplash", "author": "Catarina Duarte", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@cateduart?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/the-van-gogh-museum-building-with-a-green-lawn-ynFz9p5YcBE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(299, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(337, 46%, 48%)", "label": "LIFESTYLE", "seed": "b52bc96122d4"}}, "published_date": "2026-11-07", "word_count": 279, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "John Lewis has released its 2026 Christmas advert, a three-minute film called Gloria and Pickles. It marks the retailer's 20th Christmas TV campaign and carries a simple message: don't give up on giving.", "lead_zh": "John Lewis发布了2026年圣诞广告，这支三分钟的短片名为《Gloria and Pickles》。这是这家百货公司第20支圣诞电视广告，传达的信息很简单：别放弃用心送礼。", "preview": "The story follows a grandmother named Gloria, played by British actress Kristin Scott Thomas, who is preparing her home for her grandchildre", "preview_zh": "故事讲的是一位名叫Gloria的祖母，由英国女演员克里斯汀·斯科特·托马斯饰演。平安夜前夕，她在家准备迎接孙辈的到来，想找出自己小时候的玩具逗孩子们开心，其中包括一只叫Pickles的拖拉小狗，但孩子们并不感兴趣。就在Gloria打算放弃、直接给钱的时候，Pickles鼓励她再试", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 877, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 101.525, "size_bytes": 610128, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 318, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 103.35, "size_bytes": 621072, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 318, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 110.7, "size_bytes": 665136, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 318, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 95.35, "size_bytes": 573120, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 318, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 102.275, "size_bytes": 614592, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 318, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@c9cea96/content/data/versions/894.json", "paragraphs": ["The story follows a grandmother named Gloria, played by British actress Kristin Scott Thomas, who is preparing her home for her grandchildren on Christmas Eve. She searches for toys from her own childhood, including a pull-along dog called Pickles, but the children show little interest in them. Just as Gloria is about to give up and hand out cash instead, Pickles encourages her to keep trying.", "Gloria eventually builds a 'secret den' in her house, and the family share a memorable holiday evening playing together there. Everything used to decorate the space can be bought at John Lewis, and the film ends with the line 'Don't give up on giving.' The message suggests that thoughtful, old-fashioned gestures still matter at a time when young people are easily distracted by phone screens.", "The advert was made by Saatchi & Saatchi and directed by Lucy Forbes, while comedian Paul Whitehouse voices Pickles. Its soundtrack is Sam Fender's cover of the Rolling Stones song 'You Can't Always Get What You Want', and Mick Jagger said he was delighted to hear it. The single is sold on CD and 7-inch vinyl at John Lewis, with all profits going to children's charities.", "Pickles himself is a Fisher-Price toy called the Little Snoopy Pull-Along Toy, first launched in the 1960s and now priced at £12.99. John Lewis has sold Christmas adverts since 2007, though they only became a cultural event after 2011's The Long Wait. The retailer has reportedly considered dropping the adverts because of their high cost, but for now the tradition continues.", "Behind the story is a year-round campaign to draw shoppers back into department stores and encourage them to choose gifts carefully."], "paragraphs_zh": ["故事讲的是一位名叫Gloria的祖母，由英国女演员克里斯汀·斯科特·托马斯饰演。平安夜前夕，她在家准备迎接孙辈的到来，想找出自己小时候的玩具逗孩子们开心，其中包括一只叫Pickles的拖拉小狗，但孩子们并不感兴趣。就在Gloria打算放弃、直接给钱的时候，Pickles鼓励她再试试。", "最终Gloria在家里布置出一间“秘密基地”，一家人一起在那里度过了一个难忘的节日夜晚。布置用到的所有东西都能在John Lewis买到，片子最后打出“Don't give up on giving”（别放弃用心送礼）。这句话想说的是，在年轻人很容易被手机屏幕分心的时代，那些传统而走心的心意依然可贵。", "这支广告由Saatchi & Saatchi制作，露西·福布斯执导，喜剧演员保罗·怀特豪斯为Pickles配音。背景音乐是Sam Fender翻唱滚石乐队的《You Can't Always Get What You Want》，米克·贾格尔表示听到翻唱很开心。这首单曲以CD和7英寸黑胶两种形式在John Lewis发售，全部利润捐给儿童慈善机构。", "Pickles本尊是费雪的一款玩具，名叫Little Snoopy Pull-Along Toy，最早在上世纪60年代推出，如今售价12.99英镑。John Lewis从2007年起推出圣诞广告，但直到2011年的《漫长等待》之后才真正成为文化事件。据传因为成本高昂，这家零售商曾考虑不再拍圣诞广告，但目前这一传统仍在继续。", "故事背后是John Lewis全年持续的营销活动，希望吸引消费者重新走进百货商店、认真挑选礼物。这支广告也许解决不了孩子沉迷屏幕的问题，但它提醒观众：在礼物上花心思，是值得的。"], "body": "The story follows a grandmother named Gloria, played by British actress Kristin Scott Thomas, who is preparing her home for her grandchildren on Christmas Eve. She searches for toys from her own childhood, including a pull-along dog called Pickles, but the children show little interest in them. Just as Gloria is about to give up and hand out cash instead, Pickles encourages her to keep trying.\n\nGloria eventually builds a 'secret den' in her house, and the family share a memorable holiday evening playing together there. Everything used to decorate the space can be bought at John Lewis, and the film ends with the line 'Don't give up on giving.' The message suggests that thoughtful, old-fashioned gestures still matter at a time when young people are easily distracted by phone screens.\n\nThe advert was made by Saatchi & Saatchi and directed by Lucy Forbes, while comedian Paul Whitehouse voices Pickles. Its soundtrack is Sam Fender's cover of the Rolling Stones song 'You Can't Always Get What You Want', and Mick Jagger said he was delighted to hear it. The single is sold on CD and 7-inch vinyl at John Lewis, with all profits going to children's charities.\n\nPickles himself is a Fisher-Price toy called the Little Snoopy Pull-Along Toy, first launched in the 1960s and now priced at £12.99. John Lewis has sold Christmas adverts since 2007, though they only became a cultural event after 2011's The Long Wait. The retailer has reportedly considered dropping the adverts because of their high cost, but for now the tradition continues.\n\nBehind the story is a year-round campaign to draw shoppers back into department stores and encourage them to choose gifts carefully.", "body_zh": "故事讲的是一位名叫Gloria的祖母，由英国女演员克里斯汀·斯科特·托马斯饰演。平安夜前夕，她在家准备迎接孙辈的到来，想找出自己小时候的玩具逗孩子们开心，其中包括一只叫Pickles的拖拉小狗，但孩子们并不感兴趣。就在Gloria打算放弃、直接给钱的时候，Pickles鼓励她再试试。\n\n最终Gloria在家里布置出一间“秘密基地”，一家人一起在那里度过了一个难忘的节日夜晚。布置用到的所有东西都能在John Lewis买到，片子最后打出“Don't give up on giving”（别放弃用心送礼）。这句话想说的是，在年轻人很容易被手机屏幕分心的时代，那些传统而走心的心意依然可贵。\n\n这支广告由Saatchi & Saatchi制作，露西·福布斯执导，喜剧演员保罗·怀特豪斯为Pickles配音。背景音乐是Sam Fender翻唱滚石乐队的《You Can't Always Get What You Want》，米克·贾格尔表示听到翻唱很开心。这首单曲以CD和7英寸黑胶两种形式在John Lewis发售，全部利润捐给儿童慈善机构。\n\nPickles本尊是费雪的一款玩具，名叫Little Snoopy Pull-Along Toy，最早在上世纪60年代推出，如今售价12.99英镑。John Lewis从2007年起推出圣诞广告，但直到2011年的《漫长等待》之后才真正成为文化事件。据传因为成本高昂，这家零售商曾考虑不再拍圣诞广告，但目前这一传统仍在继续。\n\n故事背后是John Lewis全年持续的营销活动，希望吸引消费者重新走进百货商店、认真挑选礼物。这支广告也许解决不了孩子沉迷屏幕的问题，但它提醒观众：在礼物上花心思，是值得的。", "text": "The story follows a grandmother named Gloria, played by British actress Kristin Scott Thomas, who is preparing her home for her grandchildren on Christmas Eve. She searches for toys from her own childhood, including a pull-along dog called Pickles, but the children show little interest in them. Just as Gloria is about to give up and hand out cash instead, Pickles encourages her to keep trying. Gloria eventually builds a 'secret den' in her house, and the family share a memorable holiday evening playing together there. Everything used to decorate the space can be bought at John Lewis, and the film ends with the line 'Don't give up on giving.' The message suggests that thoughtful, old-fashioned gestures still matter at a time when young people are easily distracted by phone screens. The advert was made by Saatchi & Saatchi and directed by Lucy Forbes, while comedian Paul Whitehouse voices Pickles. Its soundtrack is Sam Fender's cover of the Rolling Stones song 'You Can't Always Get What You Want', and Mick Jagger said he was delighted to hear it. The single is sold on CD and 7-inch vinyl at John Lewis, with all profits going to children's charities. Pickles himself is a Fisher-Price toy called the Little Snoopy Pull-Along Toy, first launched in the 1960s and now priced at £12.99. John Lewis has sold Christmas adverts since 2007, though they only became a cultural event after 2011's The Long Wait. The retailer has reportedly considered dropping the adverts because of their high cost, but for now the tradition continues. Behind the story is a year-round campaign to draw shoppers back into department stores and encourage them to choose gifts carefully.", "vocab": [{"word": "advert", "pos": "noun", "zh": "广告", "note": "英式说法，美式常用 ad/commercial", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pull-along", "pos": "adj", "zh": "拖拉式的", "note": "指可以拉着走的玩具", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "show little interest", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "没什么兴趣", "note": "比 not interested 更书面", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "give up", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "放弃", "note": "后接名词或动名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "secret den", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "秘密基地", "note": "den 指孩子玩耍的小天地", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "thoughtful", "pos": "adj", "zh": "用心的、体贴的", "note": "常修饰礼物、举动", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "distracted", "pos": "adj", "zh": "分心的", "note": "be distracted by 被……分心", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "soundtrack", "pos": "noun", "zh": "配乐", "note": "影视广告的背景音乐", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cover", "pos": "noun", "zh": "翻唱版本", "note": "a cover of a song", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "profits", "pos": "noun", "zh": "利润", "note": "常用复数，go to 捐给", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cultural event", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "文化事件", "note": "指引发广泛关注的现象", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "worth the effort", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "值得付出", "note": "固定搭配，表示值得一做", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T01:02:45.259729", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.375, "sm": 275, "em": 374, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "story", "s": 0.375, "e": 0.762, "sm": 375, "em": 762, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "follows", "s": 0.762, "e": 1.112, "sm": 762, "em": 1112, "cs": 10, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "a", "s": 1.113, "e": 1.175, "sm": 1112, "em": 1175, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "grandmother", "s": 1.175, "e": 1.775, "sm": 1175, "em": 1774, "cs": 20, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "named", "s": 1.775, "e": 2.062, "sm": 1775, "em": 2